INSERT INTO `contact_messages` VALUES (1,'Sri Madhumitha','srimadhumitha0211@gmail.com','7010998832','Api testing','2026-02-04 01:36:00','2026-02-04 01:36:00'),(2,'Pranay Mandadapu','mpranay2017@gmail.com','4146288883','Dear Editorial Team,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in joining the Reviewer Board for the Fifth Dimension research Publication .\n\nI am a Full Stack Engineer and Researcher specializing in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Vision, and Deep Learning. My research focuses on hybrid deep learning pipelines (YOLOv8 + Inception-ResNetV2) for automated Human Activity Recognition (HAR). I have recently submitted a manuscript on this topic to the Cureus Journal of Medical Science.\n\nI am available to provide timely and constructive reviews for manuscripts in the following areas:\n\nArtificial Intelligence & Machine Learning\n\nComputer Vision & Image Processing\n\nInformation Technology Applications\n\nDeep Learning Architectures\n\nI am committed to supporting the journal\'s peer review process and maintaining high publication standards.','2026-02-07 02:12:19','2026-02-07 02:12:19'),(3,'Shalini Saksena','saksena.shalini@gmail.com','9810450702','I am working on finalising an article, which looks at the available evidence on the net impact of the use of AI across different sectors in an Economy (such Agriculture, Manufacturing, Electricity Grid etc.) on Environmental Stress (Carbon dioxide emissions). I want to know if this topic falls under the purview of the Journal \'Indian Journal of Computer Science and Technology\' (indjcst) ?','2026-02-07 14:21:11','2026-02-07 14:21:11'),(4,'PRABHAT','prabhatkumariitr@gmail.com','9897373501','Respected Sir/Ma’am,\n\nI would like to inquire about the possibility of publishing a research paper in the November 2025 issue (Computer Science Engineering domain).\n\nThanking you.\n\nRegards,\n\nDr. Prabhat','2026-02-12 12:51:41','2026-02-12 12:51:41'),(5,'Ulbossyn Omirali','ulbossyn.omirali@narxoz.kz','7059656145','Good afternoon.\nCould you please send an invoice for my article:\nhttps://www.indjcst.com/archives/paper-details?paperid=275&papertitle=conceptual-design-of-idgms-based-on-multi-agent-technologies\n\nThe publication fee was paid by my organization, and our accounting department requires closing documents, such as an official invoice, for their records.\nI would appreciate it if you could send the invoice at your earliest convenience.\nThank you in advance for your assistance.','2026-02-18 10:41:28','2026-02-18 10:41:28'),(6,'Dr. G. N. R. PRASAD','gnrp@cbit.ac.in','9885191683','Sir, I am a professor in a Engg college, Hyderabad. We are planning to conduct a National conf. on the month of April 2026.  Around 30 articles will be published in your journal. We would like to talk regarding this.\nThank you','2026-03-19 17:48:33','2026-03-19 17:48:33'),(7,'Jiaxin Li','lijiaxin203@mails.ucas.ac.cn','1580309361','Formal Complaint of Plagiarism – Your Paper \"Hyperspectral Image Enhancement Using Enhanced Deep Image Prior\" (Paper ID: 295)\n\nDear Editor-in-Chief,\n\nI am writing to formally report a case of plagiarism involving an article published in your journal. My name is Jiaxin Li, and I am the first author of the paper:\n“Enhanced Deep Image Prior for Unsupervised Hyperspectral Image Super-Resolution” Published in IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing (TGRS),\nAvailable at: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/10845210\n\n\nIt has come to my attention that the article:“Hyperspectral Image Enhancement Using Enhanced Deep Image Prior” (Paper ID: 295)\nPublished in Indian Journal of Computer Science and Technology contains substantial text, methodology, and conceptual similarities to my aforementioned TGRS paper without proper attribution, citation, or consent. The similarities include, but are not limited to, the core technical framework (“Enhanced Deep Image Prior”), the experimental setup, and key textual passages.\n\n\nI request that you kindly investigate this matter promptly in accordance with your journal’s ethical policies and take appropriate action, which may include retraction of the infringing article.\n\n\nPlease do not hesitate to contact me should you require any further information or documentation.\nThank you for your attention to this serious matter.\n\n\nSincerely,\n\nJiaxin Li','2026-03-21 05:38:37','2026-03-21 05:38:37'),(8,'mansi','mansipattanwal@gmail.com','9306377327','I am trying to submit my article. It repeatedly shows you article sumission failed. How can I submit my article.','2026-03-22 07:12:34','2026-03-22 07:12:34'),(9,'Prashant Kumar Baheti','pra123_baheti@rediffmail.com','9829086145','INDJCST-01973: A Secure and Decentralized Blockchain-Based Electronic Voting Framework with Smart Contract Enforcement\nLokesh Kumar Garg, Sumit Kumar, Prashant Kumar Baheti\nin the Indian Journal of Computer Science and Technology\nRequest for a fee-paid receipt.\nPlease share the fee paid receipt.','2026-03-28 12:47:12','2026-03-28 12:47:12'),(10,'Patrick MARIE','patricklmarie@gmail.com','0674403982','I have written a book named “Modern Web Cartography”, which has recently been published by Apress, and I would like to make your organization and its readers aware of it. \n\nIf you would like to review the book for possible publication of an assessment, please send me your name and email address. I will arrange for Apress to provide you with an electronic copy.\n\nThe book explores the use of open-source technologies for building interactive maps and web-based cartographic applications.\n\nIt first presents an overview of the ecosystem surrounding OpenStreetMap and several related open-source tools widely used for web mapping, including Overpass API, Nominatim, Leaflet, and Folium.\n\nThen, through a series of practical examples, it demonstrates how these tools can be used to access geographic data from the OpenStreetMap database, perform geocoding and reverse geocoding operations, and create interactive maps for web applications. The examples illustrate both client-side approaches using JavaScript and the Leaflet library, and server-side approaches using Python and the Folium library.\n\nThe pedagogical approach is progressive: it begins with simple use cases focusing on individual tools and then moves on to more advanced scenarios combining several components of the OpenStreetMap ecosystem.\n\nThe book is intended for web developers interested in integrating interactive cartographic functionality into their applications, as well as for readers wishing to gain a broader understanding of the OpenStreetMap environment and the role of open-source tools in modern web cartography.\n\nPublication details:\n- Author: Patrick Marie\n- Title: Modern Web Cartography - Open Source Map Solutions with OpenStreetMap, Overpass, Nominatim, Leaflet and Folium\n- Publisher: Apress\n- Year: 2026\n- Length: 540 pages\n\nMore information about the publication is available at:\nhttps://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/979-8-8688-2335-0','2026-03-30 12:50:27','2026-03-30 12:50:27'),(11,'Yadwinder singh Bains','yadwinderbains62@gmail.com','7652916016','Hi yadwinder here \nIn how much time you should publish the paper and how much is publishing fees','2026-04-04 07:00:42','2026-04-04 07:00:42'),(12,'Rishita','rishita.m8@gmail.com','9821702730','I am writing to inquire about the paper submissions to the next upcoming issue. I recently became aware of the journal and found it highly relevant to my research work.\n\nI wanted to understand the time taken for review, deadlines for next issue for the same.\n\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n\nWarm regards,\nRishita Makde','2026-04-09 09:52:33','2026-04-09 09:52:33'),(13,'Alok Kushwaha','kushwahaalok025@gmail.com','9137479236','My paper was published in the Journal of INDJCST, but my DOI link is not working. I am getting not found when I clicked on it.','2026-04-14 15:46:25','2026-04-14 15:46:25'),(14,'Pooja Sharma','ps3340723@gmail.com','7017930216','I want to published my review article in your publication','2026-04-22 08:30:40','2026-04-22 08:30:40'),(15,'DR. Mukta Ranjan Singha','mrsingham@yahoo.com','9957902404','Please create an account for me in your Journal, such that I can submit my research papers.','2026-04-25 04:20:19','2026-04-25 04:20:19'),(16,'Somay Singh','somaysingh2306@gmail.com','9911671463','I am not able to upload my paper as the author login page is not working.','2026-05-06 17:27:26','2026-05-06 17:27:26');
