24 24\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden>\r\n            <path d=\"M12 2v6M12 16v6M4 8l8 8 8-8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"></path>\r\n          </svg>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <strong>Plagiarism Protection &amp; COPE Compliance</strong>\r\n            <p class=\"small\">INDJCST screens all submissions for plagiarism and follows COPE\'s best practices. Ethical expectations — including consent for data use — are enforced for all published research.</p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </li>\r\n\r\n        <li class=\"feature\">\r\n          <svg class=\"icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden>\r\n            <path d=\"M3 12h18\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"></path>\r\n          </svg>\r\n          <div>\r\n            <strong>Impact Beyond Academia</strong>\r\n            <p class=\"small\">We encourage research that shapes policy and practice — especially rigorous work on <strong>ethics in data collection and usage</strong>, privacy-preserving computation, and fair data governance.</p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </li>\r\n\r\n      </ul>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <!-- Indexing & Abstracting -->\r\n    <section class=\"card\">\r\n      <h3>Indexing &amp; Abstracting</h3>\r\n      <p class=\"small\">INDJCST is indexed or discoverable through a wide range of platforms that increase visibility and citation potential. This includes Google Scholar, SSRN, Mendeley, Dimensions, WorldCat and more — making INDJCST one of the accessible choices among the <em>Best Computer Science journals</em> for a wide audience.</p>\r\n\r\n      <p class=\"small\"><strong>Platforms:</strong> Google Scholar, Scribd, ISSUU, Elsevier Mendeley, EuroPub, DRJI, Academic Keys, I2OR, ResearchBIB, SSRN, WorldCAT, Exlibris, Thomson Reuters Research ID, Semantic Scholar, Dimensions, PlumX.</p>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <!-- Publication process timeline -->\r\n    <section class=\"card\">\r\n      <h3>Our Streamlined Publication Process</h3>\r\n      <p class=\"small\">We aim to provide transparency and speed while maintaining editorial rigor. Typical timelines (author-facing):</p>\r\n      <ul class=\"small\">\r\n        <li>Submit Online: 24/7 submission through our editorial management system</li>\r\n        <li>Initial Response: Acknowledgement within 12 hours</li>\r\n        <li>Expert Review: Peer review completed in ~2 days</li>\r\n        <li>Decision Notification: Acceptance/rejection within 3 days</li>\r\n        <li>Publication &amp; Certificate: Instant PDF access and digital certificate</li>\r\n      </ul>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <!-- Article Processing Charges -->\r\n    <section class=\"card\">\r\n      <h3>Article Processing Charges (APC)</h3>\r\n      <p class=\"small\">Open-access publishing requires a minimal APC to support website hosting, DOI minting (if chosen), and continuous publication. Fees are charged only after manuscript acceptance.</p>\r\n      <table class=\"apc-table\" aria-describedby=\"apc-description\">\r\n        <thead>\r\n          <tr><th>Article Type</th><th>For Indian Authors</th><th>For Other than Indian Authors</th></tr>\r\n        </thead>\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr><td>Case Report / Original / Review</td><td>Without DOI: ₹1,200 + 18% GST<br>With DOI: ₹1,400 + 18% GST</td><td>With DOI: $80 USD</td></tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table>\r\n      <p id=\"apc-description\" class=\"small\">All fees are processed securely and the journal issues an official invoice and electronic certificate after payment.</p>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <!-- Editorial tools and features -->\r\n    <section class=\"card\">\r\n      <h3>Advanced Editorial Management System</h3>\r\n      <p class=\"small\">Authors get a personalized dashboard with real-time tracking, automated acceptance letters, copyright forms, and one-click downloads — simplifying the publication journey for busy researchers and practitioners in the field of computer science